I found a scraper that we could try to implement into our own project. 

One relevant research item I found for this project is a vote scraping tool developed by OpenStates, 
which includes a custom scraper designed specifically for extracting roll call vote data from Massachusetts House and Senate journal PDFs. 
This scraper is highly relevant to the problem because it addresses the core challenge of the project: the lack of accessible, 
structured legislative voting records. The tool parses complex and inconsistently formatted PDF files, 
extracting detailed information such as legislator names, vote types (yes, no, not voting), bill numbers, motions, and outcomes. 
By using this scraper as a starting point, we can significantly streamline the data collection process and begin building the cleaned dataset needed for analysis and visualization in Looker Studio.

https://github.com/openstates/openstates-scrapers/blob/main/scrapers/ma/votes.py
